insert into portal_settings (key, value) values ('chpms_version', 'v2'), ('chpms_readme', 'Prepared for 2nd Chance Housing Inc. • First-pass research • All information accessed 2026-11-11
• Relational tables: Organizations → Programs (org_id) → Assistance_Types / Eligibility / Program_Populations / Application_Procedures (program_id); Contacts, Service_Areas, Landlord_Partnerships (org_id); Referral_Relationships (from/to org_id); Funding_Relationships; Source_Documents (source_id); Verification_History.
• Deliverable views: Financial_Assistance_Dir, Pop_* sheets (10 populations), Landlord_Partnerships, Referral_Pathways, Funding_Map, Gaps_Opportunities, Discovery_Log.
• Verification colors: green = Verified – Current; yellow = Verified – Limited; orange = Needs Confirmation; grey = Inactive/Expired or Unverified Lead.
• Rules followed: no amounts estimated (''Not publicly disclosed''); conflicting phone numbers/addresses recorded with both values; third-party data labeled.
• Coverage is NOT exhaustive. See Discovery_Log for unresearched suburbs and open questions. Re-verify status by phone before any client referral.
Version 2 – merged with four user-supplied documents (D1–D4). See Merge_Log and Conflicts_Log. Imported claims are labeled by document (D1–D4). A claim re-checked against an official or news source this session keeps or upgrades its status. A claim where the imported document cites an official URL that was not re-fetched is ''Verified – Limited (imported)''. A claim with no checkable source is ''Needs Confirmation'' or ''Unverified Lead''. Claims contradicted by fresher evidence are rejected and listed in Merge_Log.
Note: Type counts use classification codes in Organizations!E. Outside-referral flag is inferred from Type 2/3/5 roles; confirm intake policies per org.')
on conflict (key) do update set value = excluded.value;
